From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media, dhcpcsvc: caption settings, DHCP client API and parameter change events

- Windows.Media.ClosedCaptioning.ClosedCaptionProperties: the getters were
  "semi-stub" FIXMEs that always said Default and the computed colours
  were E_NOTIMPL. The user's caption settings are read (as the
  ClosedCaption* enumeration values under
  HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\ClosedCaptioning: font
  colour, opacity, size, style and edge effect, background and region
  colour and opacity); what is not set or not valid is Default. A computed
  colour is the colour chosen, E_INVALIDARG with none chosen as Windows
  answers (Wine's test had those as todo_wine). The factory's GetIids,
  GetRuntimeClassName and GetTrustLevel were E_NOTIMPL FIXMEs.
- dhcpcsvc: DhcpCApiInitialize and DhcpCApiCleanup were FIXMEs (now
  counted; no version pointer is ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER);
  DhcpRegisterParamChange and DhcpDeRegisterParamChange were "@ stub"s:
  the event is signalled when the adapter's (or any adapter's) addresses or
  interface change, from IP Helper's change notifications.

Gate: test/capsdhcp-gate.sh (in a network namespace with a dummy
interface, test/capsdhcp-probe.c). Mutants SG_MUTANT_CAPTIONS_DEFAULT
(windows.media/captions.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_PARAM_CHANGE
(dhcpcsvc/dhcpcsvc.c). Wine's windows.media captions test: 0 todo, 0
failures (6 todo_wine removed); dhcpcsvc test: no failures.
---
--- a/dlls/dhcpcsvc/dhcpcsvc.c
+++ b/dlls/dhcpcsvc/dhcpcsvc.c
@@ -32,18 +32,47 @@
 #include "ddk/mountmgr.h"
 
 #include "wine/debug.h"
